% Problem 41. Chace vol. II pl. 63 (photograph XVIII), PDF pp. 173-174; Peet pp. 80-81 (Pl. M).
No. 41
{"Example of making a granary round, of 9"} "by 10."
"Take away thou '9 of 9, namely 1; the remainder is 8."
"Multiply 8 up to times 8; there become 64."
"Make thou the multiplication 64 up to times 10; becomes it 640."
"Add '2 of it to it; becomes it 960," {"the content of it in khar."}
"Make thou '20 of 960, namely 48; what goes, this is, into it in quadruple hekat:" {"grain, 4800 hekat."}
"Manner of the reckoning of it."
  1   8
  2   16
  4   32
\ 8   64
  1   64
\ 10  640
\ '2  320     % the '2 is half of 640, not of 64 (the scribe adds half of 640 to it)
Total 960.
  '10  96     % '10 and '20 are of 960
\ '20  48     % Peet: no tick on '20
